      ],
      "prompt": "A company exposes an API through Amazon API Gateway for submitting document-conversion jobs. Each conversion takes 2 to 10 minutes. Clients must receive an immediate acknowledgment when a job is accepted, and jobs must not be lost if the conversion backend is temporarily unavailable or overwhelmed. The company wants to minimize custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Configure the REST API with a direct AWS service integration that sends each request to an Amazon SQS queue, and have an AWS Lambda function consume the queue.",
        "B": "Configure API Gateway with a synchronous Lambda proxy integration that performs the conversion and returns the result in the response.",
        "C": "Configure API Gateway with an HTTP proxy integration to an Application Load Balancer in front of EC2 instances that perform the conversion synchronously.",
        "D": "Configure API Gateway to invoke a Lambda function that writes each job to an Amazon ElastiCache cluster, and have a fleet of EC2 worker instances poll the cache for new jobs."
